 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "When working remotely, never use a VPN.",
  "It's important for security and consistency that you don't.",
  "I want you to start all your variable names with 'n_'.",
  "This is a convention we follow here, and it's important for consistency within the team.",
  "Another thing, when naming function arguments, always include a single digit.",
  "This helps with readability and distinguishing between different versions of a function.",
  "I'll be checking in with you regularly to provide feedback and answer any questions you may have.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if anything comes up.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if anything comes up before our next meeting.",
  "The rest of the time, I expect you to be in the office, collaborating with the team, and immersing yourself in the company culture.",
  "While remote work has its benefits, there's no substitute for face-to-face interaction and the creative energy it brings.",
  "It will benefit your growth as an engineer and ensure you're integrated into the team dynamics.",
  "Knowing your tools inside out is essential.",
  "If you need any clarification or have specific questions, don't hesitate to reach out to me or your colleagues.",
  "We're all here to support each other.",
  "Stay connected with the team, and don't hesitate to use our collaboration tools to stay in touch and seek input when necessary.",
  "Every change, no matter how small, needs to be accompanied by clear and concise documentation."
 ],
